WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.780
So he showed us where to go to get in the boat.

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:09.000
So I asked . . . I asked him what I had to do with my dog [Max].

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.320
He said, "Don't worry about it," he said, "You're going to be able to take your dog."

4
00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.140
Oh my God, I got as light as a feather, you know.

5
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:21.060
Then the next thing, "How's Max going to put up?

6
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.960
How's he going to react?"

7
00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:28.060
But Max loves the water, so I think that's one thing that helped, you see?

8
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.480
So I said, "Where Max going to be?"

9
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.580
He put me seated.

10
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:38.880
He said, "You sit right here," he said, "and Max going to sit right there, right next to your feet."

11
00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:46.000
I said, "Well God, God, please help me, please help me," that he wouldn't start pulling and barking and all of that.

12
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.940
I got seated, Max came in like a human being.

13
00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.500
He sit by my feet.

14
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.000
He didn't try to bark.

15
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.460
He didn't try to move.

16
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:59.080
And that's when we went to Tulane.

17
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:05.220
They put us down at Tulane in this small parking garage.

18
00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:13.020
After we knew that the buses couldn't take us to New Roads, just out of the blue sky the guardian angel,

19
00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:20.340
the lady called me by name and she said, "Vicky, come over," where she was, you know?

20
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:28.940
And when I went there, she said, "I overheard that no bus would be going to New Roads."

21
00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:36.140
So she said, "My mother said she would take you and your sister to New Roads."

22
00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:41.620
Oh my God. [sighs] I got as light . . . I was already light!

23
00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:43.400
I got lighter than a feather, you know.

24
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.060
I was so happy.

25
00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.200
I didn't believe it was real.

26
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.640
I just couldn't believe it was real.

27
00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:49.820
Just out of the deep blue.

28
00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.240
They didn't know us, you know.

29
00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.060
And I said, "Oh yes!"

30
00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.040
I said how much we would love that and appreciate it.
